     rect (0.0,0.0) [448.0 x 2366.36] rgba=00000000
      rect (0.0,0.0) [448.0 x 2366.36] rgba=00000000
       rect (20.0,0.0) [408.0 x 2286.36] rgba=00000000
        rect (0.40799999,0.0) [407.18399999 x 1197.84] rgba=00000000
         rect (0.0,0.0) [407.18399999 x 107.0] rgba=00000000
          rect (0.0,0.0) [407.18399999 x 65.0] rgba=FF656701
           text (10.0,4.0) [143.0 x 19.0] rgba=FFFFFFFF f=17/700 "Rust's 'Vision Doc' Makes "
           text (10.0,23.0) [215.0 x 19.0] rgba=FFFFFFFF f=17/700 "Recommendations to Help Keep Rust "
           text (10.0,42.0) [48.0 x 19.0] rgba=FFFFFFFF f=17/700 "Growing"
           rect (58.0,47.0) [14.0 x 14.0] rgba=00000000
            text (15.0,0.0) [60.0 x 14.0] rgba=FFCCCC93 f=12/400 "(rust-lang.org) "
           text (77.0,42.0) [6.0 x 19.0] rgba=FFFFFFFF f=17/700 "2"
          rect (0.0,65.0) [407.18399999 x 42.0] rgba=FFF2F2F2
           text (43.0,5.0) [109.0 x 16.0] rgba=FF4D4D4D f=14/400 "Posted by EditorDavid "
           text (152.0,5.0) [196.0 x 16.0] rgba=FF4D4D4D f=14/400 "on Sunday December 21, 2025 @12:34AM"
           text (348.0,5.0) [26.0 x 16.0] rgba=FF4D4D4D f=14/400 " from "
           text (20.0,21.0) [19.0 x 16.0] rgba=FF4D4D4D f=14/400 "the "
           text (39.0,21.0) [88.0 x 16.0] rgba=FF4D4D4D f=14/400 "Rust-never-sleeps"
           text (127.0,21.0) [31.0 x 16.0] rgba=FF4D4D4D f=14/400 " dept. "
         rect (0.0,107.0) [407.18399999 x 1035.0] rgba=00000000
          rect (20.0,20.0) [367.18399999 x 1015.0] rgba=00000000
           text (0.0,0.0) [137.0 x 19.0] rgba=FF000000 f=17/400 "The team authoring the "
           text (137.0,0.0) [116.0 x 19.0] rgba=FF000000 f=17/400 "Rust 2025 Vision Doc"
           text (253.0,0.0) [101.0 x 19.0] rgba=FF000000 f=17/400 " interviewed Rust "
           text (0.0,19.0) [336.0 x 19.0] rgba=FF000000 f=17/400 "developers to find out what they liked about the language "
           text (336.0,19.0) [10.0 x 19.0] rgba=FF000000 f=17/400 "— "
           text (0.0,38.0) [81.0 x 19.0] rgba=FF000000 f=17/400 "and have now "
           text (81.0,38.0) [257.0 x 19.0] rgba=FF666600 f=17/400 "issued three recommendations "to help Rust "
           text (0.0,57.0) [98.0 x 19.0] rgba=FF666600 f=17/400 "continue to scale"
           text (98.0,57.0) [200.0 x 19.0] rgba=FF000000 f=17/400 " across domains and usage levels.""
           text (0.0,76.0) [3.0 x 19.0] rgba=00000000 f=17/400 " "
           text (0.0,95.0) [350.0 x 19.0] rgba=FF000000 f=17/400 "— Enumerate and describe Rust's design goals and integrate "
           text (0.0,114.0) [366.0 x 19.0] rgba=FF000000 f=17/400 "them into our processes, helping to ensure they are observed by "
           text (0.0,133.0) [314.0 x 19.0] rgba=FF000000 f=17/400 "future language designers and the broader ecosystem."
           text (0.0,152.0) [3.0 x 19.0] rgba=00000000 f=17/400 " "
           text (0.0,171.0) [333.0 x 19.0] rgba=FF000000 f=17/400 "— Double down on extensibility, introducing the ability for "
           text (0.0,190.0) [363.0 x 19.0] rgba=FF000000 f=17/400 "crates to influence the develop experience and the compilation "
           text (0.0,209.0) [50.0 x 19.0] rgba=FF000000 f=17/400 "pipeline."
           text (0.0,228.0) [3.0 x 19.0] rgba=00000000 f=17/400 " "
           text (0.0,247.0) [347.0 x 19.0] rgba=FF000000 f=17/400 "— Help users to navigate the crates.io ecosystem and enable "
           text (0.0,266.0) [100.0 x 19.0] rgba=FF000000 f=17/400 "smoother interop"
           text (0.0,285.0) [3.0 x 19.0] rgba=00000000 f=17/400 " "
           rect (8.0,312.0) [351.18399999 x 684.0] rgba=00000000
            text (16.0,0.0) [279.0 x 19.0] rgba=FF000000 f=17/400 "The real "empowering magic" of Rust arises from "
            text (16.0,19.0) [307.0 x 19.0] rgba=FF000000 f=17/400 "achieving a number of different attributes all at once "
            text (323.0,19.0) [10.0 x 19.0] rgba=FF000000 f=17/400 "— "
            text (16.0,38.0) [317.0 x 19.0] rgba=FF000000 f=17/400 "reliability, efficiency, low-level control, supportiveness, "
            text (16.0,57.0) [326.0 x 19.0] rgba=FF000000 f=17/400 "and so forth. It would be valuable to have a canonical list "
            text (16.0,76.0) [308.0 x 19.0] rgba=FF000000 f=17/400 "of those values that we could collectively refer to as a "
            text (16.0,95.0) [335.0 x 19.0] rgba=FF000000 f=17/400 "community and that we could use when evaluating RFCs or "
            text (16.0,114.0) [329.0 x 19.0] rgba=FF000000 f=17/400 "other proposed designs... We recommend creating an RFC "
            text (16.0,133.0) [322.0 x 19.0] rgba=FF000000 f=17/400 "that defines the goals we are shooting for as we work on "
            text (16.0,152.0) [333.0 x 19.0] rgba=FF000000 f=17/400 "Rust... One insight from our research is that we don't need "
            text (16.0,171.0) [322.0 x 19.0] rgba=FF000000 f=17/400 "to define which values are "most important". We've seen "
            text (16.0,190.0) [334.0 x 19.0] rgba=FF000000 f=17/400 "that for Rust to truly work, it must achieveallthe factors at "
            text (16.0,209.0) [36.0 x 19.0] rgba=FF000000 f=17/400 "once..."
            text (16.0,228.0) [3.0 x 19.0] rgba=00000000 f=17/400 " "
            text (16.0,247.0) [317.0 x 19.0] rgba=FF000000 f=17/400 "We recommenddoubling down on extensibilityas a core "
            text (16.0,266.0) [167.0 x 19.0] rgba=FF000000 f=17/400 "strategy. Rust's extensibility "
            text (183.0,266.0) [149.0 x 19.0] rgba=FF000000 f=17/400 "— traits, macros, operator "
            text (16.0,285.0) [72.0 x 19.0] rgba=FF000000 f=17/400 "overloading "
            text (88.0,285.0) [235.0 x 19.0] rgba=FF000000 f=17/400 "— has been key to its versatility. But that "
            text (16.0,304.0) [316.0 x 19.0] rgba=FF000000 f=17/400 "extensibility is currently concentrated in certain areas: "
            text (16.0,323.0) [323.0 x 19.0] rgba=FF000000 f=17/400 "the type system and early-stage proc macros. We should "
            text (16.0,342.0) [335.0 x 19.0] rgba=FF000000 f=17/400 "expand it to coversupportive interfaces(better diagnostics "
            text (16.0,361.0) [245.0 x 19.0] rgba=FF000000 f=17/400 "and guidance from crates) andcompilation "
            text (16.0,380.0) [316.0 x 19.0] rgba=FF000000 f=17/400 "workflow(letting crates integrate at more stages of the "
            text (16.0,399.0) [316.0 x 19.0] rgba=FF000000 f=17/400 "build process)... Doubling down on extensibility will not "
            text (16.0,418.0) [316.0 x 19.0] rgba=FF000000 f=17/400 "only make current Rust easier to use, it will enable and "
            text (16.0,437.0) [285.0 x 19.0] rgba=FF000000 f=17/400 "support Rust's use in new domains. Safety Critical "
            text (16.0,456.0) [317.0 x 19.0] rgba=FF000000 f=17/400 "applications in particular require a host of custom lints "
            text (16.0,475.0) [281.0 x 19.0] rgba=FF000000 f=17/400 "and tooling to support the associated standards. "
            text (16.0,494.0) [327.0 x 19.0] rgba=FF000000 f=17/400 "Compiler extensibility allows Rust to support those niche "
            text (16.0,513.0) [167.0 x 19.0] rgba=FF000000 f=17/400 "needs in a more general way."
            text (16.0,532.0) [3.0 x 19.0] rgba=00000000 f=17/400 " "
            text (16.0,551.0) [316.0 x 19.0] rgba=FF000000 f=17/400 "We recommend finding ways to help users navigate the "
            text (16.0,570.0) [290.0 x 19.0] rgba=FF000000 f=17/400 "crates.io ecosystem... [F]inding which crates to use "
            text (16.0,589.0) [329.0 x 19.0] rgba=FF000000 f=17/400 "presents a real obstacle when people are getting started. "
            text (16.0,608.0) [333.0 x 19.0] rgba=FF000000 f=17/400 "The Rust org maintains a carefully neutral stance, which is "
            text (16.0,627.0) [327.0 x 19.0] rgba=FF000000 f=17/400 "good, but also means that people don't have anywhere to "
            text (16.0,646.0) [318.0 x 19.0] rgba=FF000000 f=17/400 "go for advice on a good "starter set" crates... Part of the "
            text (16.0,665.0) [304.0 x 19.0] rgba=FF000000 f=17/400 "solution is enabling better interop between libraries."
           text (0.0,996.0) [3.0 x 19.0] rgba=00000000 f=17/400 " "
         rect (0.0,1162.0) [407.18399999 x 17.92] rgba=00000000
          rect (0.0,0.0) [0.0 x 0.0] rgba=00000000
          rect (40.0,17.92) [367.18399999 x 0.0] rgba=00000000
        rect (0.40799999,1197.84) [407.18399999 x 704.84] rgba=00000000
         rect (0.0,0.0) [407.18399999 x 89.0] rgba=00000000
          rect (0.0,0.0) [407.18399999 x 46.0] rgba=FF656701
           text (10.0,4.0) [230.0 x 19.0] rgba=FFFFFFFF f=17/700 "Google Sues SerpApi Over Scraping and "
           text (10.0,23.0) [126.0 x 19.0] rgba=FFFFFFFF f=17/700 "Reselling Search Data"
           rect (136.0,28.0) [14.0 x 14.0] rgba=00000000
            text (15.0,0.0) [99.0 x 14.0] rgba=FFCCCC93 f=12/400 "(searchengineland.com) "
           text (155.0,23.0) [14.0 x 19.0] rgba=FFFFFFFF f=17/700 "35"
          rect (0.0,46.0) [407.18399999 x 43.0] rgba=FFF2F2F2
           text (43.0,6.0) [50.0 x 16.0] rgba=FF4D4D4D f=14/400 "Posted by "
           text (93.0,5.0) [39.0 x 17.0] rgba=FF333333 f=14/700 "BeauHD"
           text (132.0,6.0) [192.0 x 16.0] rgba=FF4D4D4D f=14/400 "on Friday December 19, 2025 @10:30PM"
           text (324.0,6.0) [48.0 x 16.0] rgba=FF4D4D4D f=14/400 " from the "
           text (372.0,6.0) [21.0 x 16.0] rgba=FF4D4D4D f=14/400 "serp"
           text (20.0,22.0) [57.0 x 16.0] rgba=FF4D4D4D f=14/400 "ing-up-data"
           text (77.0,22.0) [31.0 x 16.0] rgba=FF4D4D4D f=14/400 " dept. "
         rect (0.0,89.0) [407.18399999 x 560.0] rgba=00000000
          rect (20.0,20.0) [367.18399999 x 540.0] rgba=00000000
           text (0.0,0.0) [367.0 x 19.0] rgba=FF000000 f=17/400 "An anonymous reader quotes a report from Search Engine Land: "
           rect (8.0,27.0) [351.18399999 x 494.0] rgba=00000000
            text (16.0,0.0) [43.0 x 19.0] rgba=FF000000 f=17/400 "Google "
            text (59.0,0.0) [25.0 x 19.0] rgba=FF666600 f=17/400 "said"
            text (84.0,0.0) [247.0 x 19.0] rgba=FF000000 f=17/400 " today that it is suing SerpApi, accusing the "
            text (16.0,19.0) [68.0 x 19.0] rgba=FF000000 f=17/400 "company of "
            text (84.0,19.0) [234.0 x 19.0] rgba=FF666600 f=17/400 "bypassing security protections to scrape, "
            text (16.0,38.0) [299.0 x 19.0] rgba=FF666600 f=17/400 "harvest, and resell copyrighted content from Google "
            text (16.0,57.0) [82.0 x 19.0] rgba=FF666600 f=17/400 "Search results"
            text (98.0,57.0) [221.0 x 19.0] rgba=FF000000 f=17/400 ". The allegations: Google said SerpApi: "
            text (16.0,76.0) [3.0 x 19.0] rgba=00000000 f=17/400 " "
            text (16.0,95.0) [326.0 x 19.0] rgba=FF000000 f=17/400 "-Circumvented Google's security measures and industry-"
            text (16.0,114.0) [158.0 x 19.0] rgba=FF000000 f=17/400 "standard crawling controls."
            text (16.0,133.0) [326.0 x 19.0] rgba=FF000000 f=17/400 "-Ignored website directives that specify whether content "
            text (16.0,152.0) [96.0 x 19.0] rgba=FF000000 f=17/400 "can be accessed."
            text (16.0,171.0) [304.0 x 19.0] rgba=FF000000 f=17/400 "-Used cloaking, rotating bot identities, and large bot "
            text (16.0,190.0) [207.0 x 19.0] rgba=FF000000 f=17/400 "networks to scrape content at scale."
            text (16.0,209.0) [314.0 x 19.0] rgba=FF000000 f=17/400 "-Took licensed content from Search features, including "
            text (16.0,228.0) [295.0 x 19.0] rgba=FF000000 f=17/400 "images and real-time data, and resold it for profit. "
            text (16.0,247.0) [3.0 x 19.0] rgba=00000000 f=17/400 " "
            text (16.0,266.0) [308.0 x 19.0] rgba=FF000000 f=17/400 "What Google is saying. "Stealthy scrapers like SerpApi "
            text (16.0,285.0) [325.0 x 19.0] rgba=FF000000 f=17/400 "override [crawling] directives and give sites no choice at "
            text (16.0,304.0) [320.0 x 19.0] rgba=FF000000 f=17/400 "all," Google wrote, calling the alleged scraping "brazen" "
            text (16.0,323.0) [325.0 x 19.0] rgba=FF000000 f=17/400 "and "unlawful." Google said SerpApi's activity "increased "
            text (16.0,342.0) [294.0 x 19.0] rgba=FF000000 f=17/400 "dramatically over the past year." [...] If Google wins, "
            text (16.0,361.0) [305.0 x 19.0] rgba=FF000000 f=17/400 "reliable SERP data could become harder to get, more "
            text (16.0,380.0) [305.0 x 19.0] rgba=FF000000 f=17/400 "expensive, or both -- especially for teams that rely on "
            text (16.0,399.0) [300.0 x 19.0] rgba=FF000000 f=17/400 "tools powered by services like SerpApi. As AI already "
            text (16.0,418.0) [306.0 x 19.0] rgba=FF000000 f=17/400 "reduces clicks and transparency, Google now appears "
            text (16.0,437.0) [329.0 x 19.0] rgba=FF000000 f=17/400 "intent on making it even harder for brands to understand "
            text (16.0,456.0) [328.0 x 19.0] rgba=FF000000 f=17/400 "how Search works, how they appear in results, and how to "
            text (16.0,475.0) [100.0 x 19.0] rgba=FF000000 f=17/400 "measure success."
           text (0.0,521.0) [3.0 x 19.0] rgba=00000000 f=17/400 " "
